<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="baa71c75">&lt;p&gt;
    A work breakdown structure (WBS)&amp;nbsp;can be developed using a top-down or bottom-up approach:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Top-down
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../practice.mgmt.proj.pm_med.base/tasks/resources/wbs_topdown.png&quot; width=&quot;300&quot; height=&quot;249&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Start with the end in mind, identify the high-level outputs
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Specify work assignments that feed these outputs
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Determine all necessary tasks for each work assignment
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Specify sub-tasks for each task as necessary
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Continue in this way until you’ve detailed your entire project
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Bottom-up
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../practice.mgmt.proj.pm_med.base/tasks/resources/wbs_bottomup.png&quot; width=&quot;300&quot; height=&quot;259&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Brainstorm all activities that you think are necessary for your project
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Group activities into a few major categories with common characteristics and eliminate any activities you do not
        have to perform
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Cross-check using the top-down approach to identify any additional activities that you overlooked in the categories
        you created
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Continue in this manner until all project work is described clearly and completely
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
